Task: Agrius convolvuli mitochondrial genome from PacBio HiFi
Date: 2026-08-28 UTC

Input
- data/inputs/collection_of_pacbio_data/err13917223/err13917223.fastqsanger.gz
- 1,318,768 reads; 14,880,429,452 bases; mean read length 11,283.6 bp; max 53,065 bp
- Input MD5 (metadata): c89a5097d200508d746c72d90c6c65c6

Assembly and consensus
- Counted canonical k=31-mers with KMC on the complete read set.
- Enriched reads with k-mer counts 2,000–2,500; Flye produced one 58,683-bp tandem disjointig.
- Self-alignment of that disjointig showed a ~15,447-bp repeated unit; one unit was used as a circular seed.
- Mapped all seed-supported HiFi reads with minimap2 (map-hifi); 3,668 primary reads and 2,113 supplementary alignments were retained.
- Built a doubled circular seed and called a Bayesian samtools consensus (min MQ 30, min BQ 20, homopolymer fix).
- Both copies of the 15,448-bp consensus were identical; direct consensus against the linear unit was identical.

Validation
- Whole-input remap to the final unit: 5,781 mapped alignments (3,668 primary; 2,113 supplementary).
- Mean depth 2,148.22x; high-quality depth (MQ/BQ >=20) min 893x; zero-depth positions 0/15,448.
- 2,190 primary reads spanned the provisional circular junction on the doubled reference.
- Final gzip test passed; final FASTA has exactly 1 record, length 15,448 bp, and 0 non-ACGT characters.
- Final compressed MD5: 7aa54fe30a344d2e74b687e26c3a47c0
